Helm Commands:

- helm repo add <repo-name> <repo-url>
- helm search repo <commands> , example - helm search repo nginx
- helm search repo wildfly --versions (to see all the versions of a chart)


** TO INSTALL a helm chart 

- helm install <Release-Name> <repo_name_in_your_local_machine/chart_name> , example - helm install nginx mybitnami/nginx 
- helm list 
- helm uninstall <release-name>

** Helm Upgrade

- helm repo add stacksimplify https://stacksimplify.github.io/helm-charts 
- helm search repo mychart1
- helm install myapp1 stacksimplify/mychart1 
- helm upgrade myapp1 stacksimplify/mychart1 --set "image.tag=2.0.0"


** Helm Histroy & status command 
- helm history <release-name>
- helm status <release-name>
- helm status myapp1 --show-resources

** Helm install/Upgrade with version 
- helm install <release-name> repo-name/chart-name --version ""
- helm status <release-name> --show-resources
- helm upgrade <release-name> <repo-name/chart-name> --version ""
- helm upgrade <release-name> <> # it will go to the latest version of the chart

** Helm Rollback
- helm history
- helm rollback <release-name> # to rollback to previous version
- helm rollback <release-name> <revision-number>

** Helm uninstall and give hsitory
- helm uninstall <release-name> --keep-history
- helm list --uninstalled
- helm history <release-name>

** Helm install with --generate-name flag (it auto generate the release-name)
- helm install <CHART-Name> --generate-name

